Now the JS. Insert the big new block: image preview + stealth/boss + sidebar watcher. Where? Logical place: after the image lightbox section (which ends before "composer 拖图片上传") for imgpreview, and before the settings panel section for stealth. To keep it simple and one insert, I'll put everything in one new section right before `/* ============================== 设置面板 ============================== */`.

But functions used by earlier code are hoisted (function declarations), and `let` variables (imgPreviewEl, bossAuto, etc.) are in TDZ only until execution reaches them — bootstrap() is called at the very end of the file, so all module-level `let`s will be initialized before any UI code runs. Wait: `bootstrap()` is called at the end; but there's code before it that might run? The IIFE body executes top-down: constants, functions, then bootstrap() at the end. So any `let` declared before bootstrap() call is initialized. Safe.

However `bindImgPreview()` is called in bootstrap; functions hoisted. Fine.

One catch: `decorateCooked` is called during render; it calls `markSmallImages` (function declaration → hoisted). Fine.

Now write the block. Contents:

```js
  /* ============================== 正文图片：缩略图 + 悬浮预览 ==============================
   *
   * 默认小图（CSS 约束），鼠标停上去在旁边浮出大图，点击仍然开灯箱。
   * 预览用 fixed 定位、不进文档流，所以不会把正文顶得跳来跳去。
   * 图源优先用 <img> 自己的 URL：缩略图就是同一张原图（只是被 CSS 缩小了），
   * 浏览器已经下载过，所以悬浮预览零延迟、也不会多发请求。
   * ================================================================= */

  let imgPreviewEl = null;
  let imgPreviewTarget = null;
  let imgPreviewTimer = null;

  const CONTENT_IMG_SEL = ".cx-turn-agent img:not(.emoji), .cx-turn-user-bubble img:not(.emoji)";

  function contentImgs(root) { return (root || document).querySelectorAll(CONTENT_IMG_SEL); }

  function fullImageUrl(img) { ... }

  function ensureImgPreview() {...}
  function placeImgPreview(anchorImg) {...}
  function showImgPreview(img) {...}
  function hideImgPreview() {...}
  function markSmallImages(root) {...}
  function bindImgPreview() {...}
```

Then stealth section, then sidebar section.

Then also: `bindLightbox`? linuxdo binds per-image click listeners inside decorateCooked for lightbox; that stays. Note the lightbox open sets gImgPreview hidden? v2ex calls hideImgPreview() in openLightbox. linuxdo's openLightbox(src) — I'll add hideImgPreview() there. Let me handle: in the new block I can't easily hook; better edit linuxdo's openLightbox to call hideImgPreview() first. Let me do that edit after.

