```
Then:
- Runtime.enable, Log.enable, Page.enable
- wait for load event (Page.loadEventFired) or just poll with Runtime.evaluate for `.codex-rail` existence up to N seconds.
- collect exceptions via Runtime.exceptionThrown; console errors via Runtime.consoleAPICalled (type error).
- run assertions via Runtime.evaluate({expression, returnByValue:true, awaitPromise:true}).

Assertions:
1. boot: `.codex-rail[data-cx-owner="linuxdo-codex-v1"]` exists && `.codex-main` exists; `document.documentElement.className` contains `codex-theme`.
2. list from stub JSON: `.cx-trow` count >= 5.
3. stealth title: document.title === "lib.rs — platform".
4. brand name: `.codex-rail [data-brand-name]`.textContent === "Codex".
5. thumb var: getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue("--ldx-thumb-w").trim() === "260px".
6. settings panel: dispatch Ctrl+, keydown; `.cx-modal` visible; sections text includes 伪装/侧边栏模式/正文图片; toggle a switch (e.g. thumbPreview) then check localStorage settings JSON has thumbPreview false; close via Esc.
7. boss: dispatch Escape twice (need to reset lastEscAt between? first Esc records; second within 450ms toggles) → check `html.classList.contains('ldx-boss-on')` and `.ldx-boss` not hidden, and its text contains "cargo test" and "Terminal". Then Escape twice again → off. Also Ctrl+Shift+H toggles.
8. sidebar mode: enable via settings or localStorage (simpler: set localStorage settings then reload? or click the toggle in the panel). Then dispatch a `mouseleave` on documentElement with relatedTarget null → wait 300ms → boss on. Then dispatch `mouseenter` on documentElement → boss off.
9. stealth off: via settings panel toggle 伪装模式 → title reverts to "<title> - Linux DO"; brand → "Linux DO".
10. detail route: navigate to /t/12345 (Page.navigate or pushState+popstate). Simplest: `Page.navigate` to http://127.0.0.1:PORT/t/12345 then wait for `.cx-turn-agent`. Check `.cx-turn-agent img` computed max-width = 260px, and hover preview: dispatch mouseover on the img → `.ldx-imgpreview.on` exists.
11. No page errors collected.

For dispatching key events: use CDP Input.dispatchKeyEvent (more realistic) — with modifiers for Ctrl+Shift+H. Escape: `Input.dispatchKeyEvent {type:"rawKeyDown", windowsVirtualKeyCode:27, key:"Escape", code:"Escape"}`. For our listener we need `e.key === "Escape"` → provide key. That works via Input domain. Also `Input.dispatchKeyEvent` type "keyDown"/"keyUp" acceptable.

For mouseleave: CDP `Input.dispatchMouseEvent` mouseMoved outside viewport is tricky; simpler to dispatch a synthetic event via Runtime.evaluate: `document.documentElement.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent('mouseleave', {bubbles:false, relatedTarget:null}))` — our listener is on root with capture=true; a synthetic event with relatedTarget null will call onLeave. That's fine for our own listener (we don't need real browser behavior).

For Ctrl+Shift+H via evaluate: `window.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keydown', {key:'h', ctrlKey:true, shiftKey:true, bubbles:true}))` — our listener is on window capture; dispatching directly on window works.

For Ctrl+, : `window.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keydown',{key:',',ctrlKey:true,bubbles:true}))`.

