content.text:
My setBoss refactor introduced a regression: the boss view now shows the class (assert "连按两下 Esc 进入伪装视图" passed? It checks `.ldx-boss` exists && !hidden && class present — it PASSED, but the log/code-lines are empty).

Look at the new setBoss:
```js
if (!document.body) return;
if (document.activeElement...) blur();
hideImgPreview();
renderBoss();          // ← renders into `.ldx-boss` — but the element doesn't exist yet on first entry!
ensureBoss().hidden = false;
```
`renderBoss()` starts with `const box = document.querySelector(".ldx-boss"); if (!box) return;` → returns early because we haven't created it. So the first time, the editor/log stay empty. Then ensureBoss() creates the empty shell and unhides it → visible but blank. Test caught it.

Previously the order was: `const box = ensureBoss(); if (on) { blur; hideImgPreview; renderBoss(); box.hidden = false; }` — ensureBoss first, then renderBoss. My "optimization" broke it.

Fix: ensureBoss() before renderBoss():
```js
if (!document.body) return;
blur...
hideImgPreview();
const box = ensureBoss();
renderBoss();
box.hidden = false;
bossAuto = false;
document.documentElement.classList.add(BOSS_CLASS);
```
Let me fix and re-run.

Good thing the test caught it — this is exactly why the harness matters.

