Simplest: in the ESC/Ctrl+Shift+H manual toggle path... we don't know if it's manual vs auto inside setBoss. Better: expose `sidebarAutoHide.forget()` that clears `shown`/`bossAuto`, and call it whenever the boss is turned off but not via restore. Implementing that inside setBoss: setBoss(false) — but restore() calls setBoss(false) — sets flags to false, which is what restore does anyway. So: in setBoss(false) branch, after clearing, call a hook: `if (sidebarAutoHide && sidebarAutoHide.forgetSticky) sidebarAutoHide.forgetSticky();`. But setBoss(false) is also called by applyVisualSettings when stealth is off; harmless.

