"forget()" count 0 because my regex escaped parens oddly. Not important — the grep showed it at line 7439 and 7559.

Now let me re-run the smoke test to validate all these changes (one more escalation). Also I should add a probe assertion for the settings modal ownership and the manual-exit-then-auto-hide case? The reviewer's item 3 (shown desync) — I fixed it with forget(); a test would be nice: 
- enable sidebarMode, mouseleave → boss on (shown=true), then manually Esc² to exit (forget clears shown), mouseenter, then mouseleave again → boss on again. That verifies the auto-hide still works after a manual exit.
Let me add that to probe.js section 6 (it currently: mouseleave → boss on; mouseenter → restore; then dblEsc manual; mouseleave/mouseenter asserts manual not auto-undone; then dblEsc off).

Add after "鼠标回来不会撤掉手动进的伪装考": `await dblEsc();` (exit manually) → mouseleave → boss on (auto-hide works again) → mouseenter → boss off. Let me insert:

```js
await dblEsc();                       // 手动退出（此时侧边栏模式仍开着）
document.documentElement.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent("mouseleave", { bubbles:false, relatedTarget:null }));
await sleep(450);
ok("手动退出后自动伪装仍然工作", document.documentElement.classList.contains("ldx-boss-on"));
document.documentElement.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent("mouseenter", { bubbles:false }));
await sleep(250);
ok("之后回来自动恢复", !document.documentElement.classList.contains("ldx-boss-on"));
```
And for the modal ownership: in the foreign phase, check that our script didn't create a modal and that a pre-existing foreign `.cx-modal` (add one to FOREIGN_PAGE) is left untouched. Let me add a foreign `.cx-modal` with id="foreign-modal" and content "旧的设置面板" to FOREIGN_PAGE, then assert:
- `document.getElementById("foreign-modal")` still exists and its innerHTML still contains "旧的设置面板" (i.e., we didn't overwrite it).
But our script only touches `.cx-modal` when settings are opened — and in the foreign phase, `openSettings()` bails because ROOT_CLASS is absent. So this assertion wouldn't prove much... unless I dispatch Ctrl+, and check the foreign modal is untouched: openSettings checks `!document.documentElement.classList.contains(ROOT_CLASS)` → returns → foreign modal untouched. Good, that's a meaningful regression test for the medium defect: dispatch Ctrl+, then assert the foreign modal content is intact and no owner-tagged modal was created.

Also add Esc-state test: with stealthKey esc2 and boss ON, pressing Esc once... hmm, hard to assert the lastEscAt reset precisely. Scenario: open settings (panel), then press Esc twice in quick succession: first closes the panel (must NOT arm), second must be "first press" (must not toggle boss). Assert `!bossOn`. That's a good test of the fix. Let me add that.

Then one final run. Let me write these probe additions, verify parse, and run.

